timestamp_provenance: "created_at and written_at are observed wall-clock CST at write time; no content timestamp runs ahead of the filesystem (review finding 10)."
status: "draft_unverified"
claims_theorem_status: false
scope_statement: >-
  This file defines four formulation classes and a machine-checkable disjointness relation.
  It asserts no theorem, no counterexample, no numerical result, and no literature claim as
  established. Every literature pointer is marked unresolved pending ledger L0/L1. Field values
  marked provisional are owned by the downstream schema nodes (F1 for AF-WCC-VAC-GEN, F2 for the
  two AF-SCC classes) and must be replaced, not inherited silently.
reconstruction_note: >-
  Reconstructed from research_map/ASTRA_HANDOFF.md:30 (hard decision 1) because the map marked F0
  done/passed while research_map/formulation_taxonomy.yaml did not exist (see
  runtime/state/checkpoint_log.jsonl#ckpt-20260911-231750).

class_ids:
  - "AF-WCC-VAC-GEN"
  - "AF-SCC-C2-VAC-GEN"
  - "AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN"
  - "AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Class-scope adjudication 2026-09-12 (controller directive astra-classscope-02).
# The frozen four class_ids above are the ONLY class ids in this taxonomy.
# Candidate readings that would otherwise become class ids are registered here
# as VARIANTS of a parent class: {parent_class, variant_id, definition,
# evidence, status}. A variant is not a class and must never be cited as one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
class_scope_adjudication:
  directive: "astra-classscope-02"
  decided_at: "2026-09-12T00:15:00+08:00"
  decision: >-
    new class ids are rejected pending Human PI. Two candidate readings are registered as
    variants of their parent class instead: the set-based visibility reading (parent_class
    AF-WCC-VAC-GEN, variant_id SET) and the horizon-localized C0 reading (parent_class
    AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN, variant_id CH). F1 carries ONE canonical visibility predicate -
    the single-q tail predicate - and the set-based form is recorded there as a variant
    pointer, never as a second predicate.
  resolved_divergences:
    - id: D1
      status: resolved
      resolution: "F0 WCC conclusion text amended to the single-q tail predicate; the set-based reading is variant SET"
    - id: D3
      status: resolved
      resolution: "the comeager quantifier is now stated explicitly in each class conclusion text and bound before the data; confirmed discharged for ALL FOUR classes, including AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH, whose conclusion text carried the demoted set-based wording until rev5 (worker-16 B-16F0-2 / worker-082 W082-F-02)"
  supersedes:
    wcc_text_sha256_before: "66bf917bd368ebd96ee46baa31fb435df106cb4e10152fa0baee8bdd51dfc232"
    wcc_text_before: "the set-based reading: 'every future-inextendible causal geodesic contained in J-(I+) is complete' (prose only; the hash above is the artifact hash this revision supersedes)"
    finding: "worker-01 F0R-01 (accepted): the lead's first rev-bump put prose under a key named sha256; repaired here"
  authority: "controller adjudication; variant finding accepted, class-id creation deferred to Human PI"

variants:
  - parent_class: "AF-WCC-VAC-GEN"
    variant_id: "SET"
    definition: >-
      replaces the single-q tail predicate by the set-based condition: a future-inextendible causal
      geodesic is visible from I+ iff gamma([0,T)) is contained in the union of J^-(q) over all q in
      I+ (intersected with M). Strictly stronger than the parent class: gamma outside the union
      implies no single q sees a tail of gamma, but not conversely.
    evidence:
      - "artifacts/formulation/variants/AF-WCC-VAC-GEN.variant-SET.delta.json"
      - "artifacts/formulation/evidence/taxonomy_consistency.json"
      - "artifacts/formulation/reviews/R1_af_wcc_review.json"
    status: "registered_variant_not_written"
    falsifier: >-
      show the two readings equivalent - every incomplete geodesic contained in the union has a tail
      inside J^-(q) for some single q - which would collapse the variant and clear D1 by proof rather
      than by wording.
  - parent_class: "AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN"
    variant_id: "CH"
    definition: >-
      horizon-localized C0 reading: the maximal development is inextendible as a continuous
      Lorentzian manifold ACROSS ITS CAUCHY HORIZON, rather than at any future boundary.
      Strictly weaker than the parent class (a subset of extensions suffices to refute it).
    evidence:
      - "artifacts/formulation/variants/AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN.variant-CH.delta.json"
      - "ledger/theorems.jsonl#D-002"
      - "ledger/theorems.jsonl#T-301"
    status: "registered_variant_not_written"
    falsifier: >-
      show that every future extension of an AF development crosses a Cauchy horizon, which would make
      the two statements equivalent and let T-301 bear on the frozen broad class.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared vocabulary. Downstream schemas (F1, F2) MUST reference these slot names
# instead of redefining them, so cross-class linting is decidable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
field_vocabulary:
  family:
    allowed: ["WCC", "SCC"]
    meaning: "WCC = visibility/asymptotic-predictability conclusion; SCC = inextendibility conclusion."
  matter_model:
    allowed: ["vacuum", "massless_scalar_field"]
    meaning: "vacuum = Ricci-flat, T=0, Lambda=0; massless_scalar_field = Einstein-massless-scalar-field system."
  symmetry:
    allowed: ["none_assumed", "spherical"]
    meaning: "spherical = SO(3) isometry with 2-sphere orbits and a regular center (symmetry-reduced data space)."
  asymptotics:
    allowed: ["asymptotically_flat_3p1"]
    meaning: "3+1 dimensional, one asymptotically flat end, conformal completion with I+, I-, i0 and a complete I+ unless the class states otherwise."
  regularity_token:
    allowed: ["C2", "C0", null]
    rule: "exactly one token iff family == SCC; null (absent) iff family == WCC."
    meaning_C2: "forbidden extensions are C2 Lorentzian extensions solving the field equations, and a fortiori every smoother class contained in C2 (C^k for k>=2, C^infinity, analytic). It does NOT forbid C^{1,1} or H^2_loc extensions: those are strictly larger classes, so excluding C2 does not exclude them (review HF-02). A statement that also forbids them is stronger and must be classified explicitly."
    meaning_C0: "forbidden extensions are C0 (continuous-metric) Lorentzian extensions; strictly stronger than the C2 conclusion when the data class and genericity notion are identical."
  genericity_kind:
    allowed: ["baire_residual", "dense_open", "measure_one", "provisional_baire_residual", "unresolved"]
    rule: "a generic-quantified claim must name genericity_kind AND genericity_topology; 'generic' alone is not a machine-readable value. 'provisional_*' tokens are placeholders owned by F1/F2 and must not be read as frozen values."
  genericity_topology:
    allowed: ["unresolved", "named_by_F1", "named_by_F2"]
    rule: "the topology or measure space in which genericity is defined; must be named before any theorem-status claim."
  conclusion_type:
    allowed:
      - "weak_cosmic_censorship"
      - "strong_cosmic_censorship_C2"
      - "strong_cosmic_censorship_C0"
    rule: "one class -> exactly one conclusion_type; strong_cosmic_censorship_C2 and _C0 are distinct values and must never be merged into a single regularity token (guards G3)."

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The four classes. `axes` carries the disjointness-relevant values and is
# machine-checked; prose fields carry hypotheses, exclusions, obstructions.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
classes:

  "AF-WCC-VAC-GEN":
    label: "Asymptotically flat weak cosmic censorship, vacuum, generic data"
    axes:
      family: "WCC"
      matter_model: "vacuum"
      symmetry: "none_assumed"
      asymptotics: "asymptotically_flat_3p1"
      regularity_token: null
      genericity_kind: "provisional_baire_residual"
      conclusion_type: "weak_cosmic_censorship"
    genericity_value_status: "provisional_owned_by_F1"
    hypotheses:
      - id: "H1"
        text: "3+1 dimensional spacetime; Lambda = 0."
        machine_checkable: true
      - id: "H2"
        text: "Matter model is vacuum: T = 0 and the metric solves the vacuum Einstein equations."
        machine_checkable: true
      - id: "H3"
        text: "Initial data (Sigma, h, K) satisfies the vacuum constraint equations, has one asymptotically flat end, and the maximal globally hyperbolic development (MGHD) exists."
        machine_checkable: true
      - id: "H4"
        text: "Data is generic in a named topology on the weighted Sobolev data space; the topology and the weighted spaces (s, delta) are owned by F1 and are unresolved here."
        machine_checkable: false
        unresolved: true
        owned_by: "F1"
      - id: "H5"
        text: "No symmetry is assumed: the data are not restricted to a spherical or axisymmetric family."
        machine_checkable: true
    conclusion:
      type: "weak_cosmic_censorship"
      text: >-
        For every admissible (s,delta) there is a comeager set G_{s,delta} of data such that for every
        data set in G_{s,delta}, the MGHD admits a conformal completion with a complete future null
        infinity I+ (all null generators complete), and no future-inextendible causal geodesic of
        finite affine length is visible from I+. Visibility uses the single-q TAIL predicate: gamma is
        visible from I+ iff there exist q in I+ and t0 in [0,T) such that the tail gamma([t0,T)) is
        contained in J^-(q) intersect M. This is a definition, not an asserted equivalence with any
        other formulation (review HF-06). The set-based reading (gamma contained in the union of
        J^-(q) over all q in I+) is strictly stronger; it is registered as variant `SET` of this
        class in the `variants:` block below and in artifacts/formulation/VARIANT_REGISTRY.json. It
        is NOT a separate class, and the two readings must never be interchanged.
      forbidden_inflation: "Does not assert inextendibility of the MGHD, and does not assert anything about extendibility in any regularity class."
    candidate_consequences:
      - id: "C1"
        text: "the black-hole region B = M \\ J-(I+) has non-empty interior whenever the development is future-incomplete"
        status: "unresolved_pending_L0_L1"
        note: >-
          NOT part of the definition and not asserted as equivalent to WCC (review finding 2). It is
          listed so F1 can decide whether to adopt it as a theorem-level consequence with a source and
          the extra hypotheses it needs (e.g. trapped-surface formation). Until then it may not be used
          as a classification predicate.
    exclusions:
      - "Any non-vacuum matter model (scalar, electromagnetic, fluid), including electrovacuum."
      - "Non-zero cosmological constant (Lambda != 0) and non-asymptotically-flat ends."
      - "Restricted symmetry classes (spherical, axisymmetric), which have their own classes."
      - "Strong cosmic censorship in either regularity: different conclusion_type."
    known_obstruction:
      status: "unresolved_pending_L0_L1"
      text: >-
        Literature pointer only, not verified here: the class contains non-generic exact black-hole
        families (e.g. subextremal Kerr) whose maximal analytic extensions cross a Cauchy horizon;
        whether that constitutes an obstruction depends on the genericity clause H4, which F1 owns.
    test_cases:
      positive:
        id: "F0-P1"
        description: "A generic one-parameter family of vacuum initial data for a perturbed subextremal black hole (no matter field)."
        decisive_hypotheses: ["H2", "H5"]
        expected_classification: "AF-WCC-VAC-GEN"
      negative:
        id: "F0-N1"
        description: "Spherically symmetric massless scalar-field collapse data."
        decisive_hypotheses: ["H2"]
        expected_classification: "AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH"
      negative_2:
        id: "F0-N2"
        description: "Exactly subextremal Kerr data presented without any genericity statement."
        decisive_hypotheses: ["H4"]
        expected_classification: "excluded_by:genericity (not silently accepted as a generic-instance claim)"
    provenance:
      source: "research_map/ASTRA_HANDOFF.md:30 (hard decision 1)"
      literature_status: "unresolved_pending_L1"
      schema_owner: "F1 (artifact schemas/af_wcc_vacuum.yaml)"

  "AF-SCC-C2-VAC-GEN":
    label: "Asymptotically flat strong cosmic censorship, C2 regularity, vacuum, generic data"
    axes:
      family: "SCC"
      matter_model: "vacuum"
      symmetry: "none_assumed"
      asymptotics: "asymptotically_flat_3p1"
      regularity_token: "C2"
      genericity_kind: "provisional_baire_residual"
      conclusion_type: "strong_cosmic_censorship_C2"
    genericity_value_status: "provisional_owned_by_F2"
    hypotheses:
      - id: "H1"
        text: "3+1 dimensional; Lambda = 0; vacuum Einstein equations."
        machine_checkable: true
      - id: "H2"
        text: "Initial data satisfies the vacuum constraints, has one asymptotically flat end, and has an MGHD."
        machine_checkable: true
      - id: "H3"
        text: "Data is generic in a named topology; the topology and weighted data spaces are owned by F2 and are unresolved here."
        machine_checkable: false
        unresolved: true
        owned_by: "F2"
      - id: "H4"
        text: "The conclusion is quantified over extensions of regularity C2 (and a fortiori any higher regularity)."
        machine_checkable: true
    conclusion:
      type: "strong_cosmic_censorship_C2"
      text: >-
        For every admissible (s,delta) there is a comeager set G_{s,delta} of data such that for every
        data set in G_{s,delta}, the MGHD is future-inextendible as a C2 Lorentzian manifold
        with C2 metric solving the vacuum Einstein equations: it admits no isometric embedding into a
        larger spacetime of that regularity. The comeager quantifier is part of the statement and is
        bound before the data; 'generic' alone is not a readable substitute for it.
      forbidden_inflation: "Do not restate as C0-inextendibility; do not restate as weak cosmic censorship."
    exclusions:
      - "Non-vacuum matter models (electrovacuum, scalar, fluid)."
      - "An AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN claim (a stronger conclusion at lower regularity); a C0 result must never be downgraded into this class."
      - "Non-generic families such as exactly subextremal Kerr data; these are excluded by H3, not by a hidden class merge."
      - "Spherically symmetric scalar-field classes."
    known_obstruction:
      status: "unresolved_pending_L0_L1"
      text: >-
        Literature pointer only, not verified here: exact subextremal Kerr vacuum solutions are
        reported to admit smooth extensions of the MGHD across the Cauchy horizon, which is the
        standard reason the genericity clause is required for the C2 class. The same literature
        reports the analogous electrovacuum statement for exact charged black holes; that is outside
        this vacuum class by matter model and is recorded here only as a pointer. The scope of each
        statement (which initial-data family, which extension) must be pinned down by L1 before it
        is used as a theorem or counterexample.
    test_cases:
      positive:
        id: "F0-P2"
        description: "A residual (Baire-generic) family of vacuum perturbations of subextremal Kerr data, with the topology named."
        decisive_hypotheses: ["H3"]
        expected_classification: "AF-SCC-C2-VAC-GEN"
      negative:
        id: "F0-N3"
        description: "Exactly subextremal Kerr data with no genericity statement."
        decisive_hypotheses: ["H3"]
        expected_classification: "excluded_by:genericity (non-generic family, not a generic-instance counterexample)"
      negative_2:
        id: "F0-N4"
        description: "A claim that proves only C0-inextendibility and is filed under this class."
        decisive_hypotheses: ["H4"]
        expected_classification: "rejected_by:conclusion_inflation_direction (a C0 result is stronger and must be filed under AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN, or both, never downgraded)"
    provenance:
      source: "research_map/ASTRA_HANDOFF.md:30 (hard decision 1)"
      literature_status: "unresolved_pending_L1"
      schema_owner: "F2a (artifact schemas/af_scc_c2_vacuum.yaml)"

  "AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN":
    label: "Asymptotically flat strong cosmic censorship, C0 regularity, vacuum, generic data"
    axes:
      family: "SCC"
      matter_model: "vacuum"
      symmetry: "none_assumed"
      asymptotics: "asymptotically_flat_3p1"
      regularity_token: "C0"
      genericity_kind: "provisional_baire_residual"
      conclusion_type: "strong_cosmic_censorship_C0"
    genericity_value_status: "provisional_owned_by_F2"
    hypotheses:
      - id: "H1"
        text: "3+1 dimensional; Lambda = 0; vacuum Einstein equations."
        machine_checkable: true
      - id: "H2"
        text: "Initial data satisfies the vacuum constraints, has one asymptotically flat end, and has an MGHD."
        machine_checkable: true
      - id: "H3"
        text: "Data is generic in a named topology; the topology and weighted data spaces are owned by F2 and are unresolved here."
        machine_checkable: false
        unresolved: true
        owned_by: "F2"
      - id: "H4"
        text: "The conclusion is quantified over C0 extensions: no continuous-metric extension of the MGHD exists. Definition subtlety (regularity of the embedding versus regularity of the metric) is flagged unresolved and must be fixed by F2/L1."
        machine_checkable: false
        unresolved: true
    conclusion:
      type: "strong_cosmic_censorship_C0"
      text: >-
        For every admissible (s,delta) there is a comeager set G_{s,delta} of data such that for every
        data set in G_{s,delta}, the MGHD is future-inextendible as a C0 (continuous-metric)
        Lorentzian manifold: it admits no isometric embedding into a larger spacetime whose metric
        extends continuously. The comeager quantifier is part of the statement and is bound before the
        data; the earlier phrasing 'for every data set in the class' is withdrawn as ambiguous.
      forbidden_inflation: "Do not weaken to C2-inextendibility; do not restate as weak cosmic censorship."
    exclusions:
      - "Non-vacuum matter models."
      - "Claims that establish only C2-inextendibility (weaker conclusion, belongs to AF-SCC-C2-VAC-GEN)."
      - "Non-generic exact black-hole families (excluded by H3)."
      - "Spherically symmetric scalar-field classes."
    known_obstruction:
      status: "unresolved_pending_L0_L1"
      text: >-
        Literature pointer only, not verified here: because smooth extensions of exact subextremal
        Kerr/Reissner-Nordstrom data exist across the Cauchy horizon, the C0 class is expected to
        require genericity just as the C2 class does. The modern C0-inextendibility results and the
        precise class of data they cover must be supplied by L1.
    test_cases:
      positive:
        id: "F0-P3"
        description: "A residual family of vacuum perturbations of a subextremal black hole for which a published C0-inextendibility result is cited with an artifact hash."
        decisive_hypotheses: ["H3", "H4"]
        expected_classification: "AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN"
      negative:
        id: "F0-N5"
        description: "A theorem whose conclusion is only C2-inextendibility."
        decisive_hypotheses: ["H4"]
        expected_classification: "AF-SCC-C2-VAC-GEN (weaker class; filing it here would be conclusion inflation)"
      negative_2:
        id: "F0-N6"
        description: "Exactly subextremal Kerr data without a genericity statement."
        decisive_hypotheses: ["H3"]
        expected_classification: "excluded_by:genericity"
    provenance:
      source: "research_map/ASTRA_HANDOFF.md:30 (hard decision 1)"
      literature_status: "unresolved_pending_L1"
      schema_owner: "F2b (artifact schemas/af_scc_c0_vacuum.yaml)"

  "AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH":
    label: "Asymptotically flat weak cosmic censorship, massless scalar field, spherical symmetry"
    axes:
      family: "WCC"
      matter_model: "massless_scalar_field"
      symmetry: "spherical"
      asymptotics: "asymptotically_flat_3p1"
      regularity_token: null
      genericity_kind: "unresolved"
      conclusion_type: "weak_cosmic_censorship"
    genericity_value_status: "unresolved_pending_L1"
    hypotheses:
      - id: "H1"
        text: "3+1 dimensional; Lambda = 0; Einstein equations coupled to a massless scalar field."
        machine_checkable: true
      - id: "H2"
        text: "Spherical symmetry: the data are SO(3)-symmetric with 2-sphere orbits and a regular center, so the data space is symmetry-reduced."
        machine_checkable: true
      - id: "H3"
        text: "Initial data (characteristic or Cauchy, as fixed by the source) is asymptotically flat with one end, and has an MGHD."
        machine_checkable: true
      - id: "H4"
        text: "Genericity notion for the symmetry-reduced data space (dense-open versus full-measure) is unresolved and must be named before any claim is filed."
        machine_checkable: false
        unresolved: true
        owned_by: "L0/L1 (no F-node owns this class in the current map)"
    conclusion:
      type: "weak_cosmic_censorship"
      text: >-
        For a comeager set G of data in the class, chosen before and independently of the data,
        every member's MGHD admits I+ and there is NO visible singularity from I+: for every
        future-inextendible causal geodesic gamma of finite affine length, for every q in I+ and
        every t0 in [0,T), the tail gamma([t0,T)) is not contained in J^-(q) intersect M. The
        singularities that form are hidden behind an event horizon and no singularity is visible
        from I+. [rev5: D1/D3 discharge for this class. The superseded set-based wording
        contained-in-J-(I+) is the variant SET predicate and is NOT this class's predicate.]
      forbidden_inflation: "Does not assert inextendibility, and the spherical symmetry may not be dropped (that is a different, open class)."
    exclusions:
      - "Vacuum data (no scalar field)."
      - "Non-spherical data: symmetry release is a different class and is forbidden as a transfer."
      - "Massive or charged scalar fields; Lambda != 0."
      - "Exactly critical/self-similar data presented as generic without a genericity statement."
    known_obstruction:
      status: "unresolved_pending_L0_L1"
      text: >-
        Literature pointer only, not verified here: the class is associated with the
        Christodoulou program on spherical scalar-field collapse (including reported naked-singularity
        examples at critically tuned, non-generic data). Which of these statements is a theorem, and
        under which genericity notion, must be supplied by L1 with primary-source scope quotes.
    test_cases:
      positive:
        id: "F0-P4"
        description: "A generic family of smooth spherically symmetric massless-scalar Cauchy data (sub- or supercritical amplitude) in the class."
        decisive_hypotheses: ["H1", "H2"]
        expected_classification: "AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH"
      negative:
        id: "F0-N7"
        description: "A vacuum-class claim whose descriptor contains no scalar field, illustrated by Schwarzschild data. The data also solve the scalar system with phi = 0, so the descriptor (not the data set) is decisive here; see the disjointness scope note."
        decisive_hypotheses: ["H1"]
        expected_classification: "AF-WCC-VAC-GEN"
      negative_2:
        id: "F0-N8"
        description: "Non-spherical massless-scalar data."
        decisive_hypotheses: ["H2"]
        expected_classification: "excluded_by:symmetry_release (no class in this taxonomy; must be opened as a new class, not filed here)"
    provenance:
      source: "research_map/ASTRA_HANDOFF.md:30 (hard decision 1)"
      literature_status: "unresolved_pending_L1"
      schema_owner: "NO F-NODE IN CURRENT MAP (coverage gap)"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pairwise disjointness. Every one of the 6 unordered pairs must differ on at
# least one named decisive axis; validate_taxonomy.py checks the axis values.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
disjointness_scope: "class descriptors (axis vectors), not data-space disjointness"
disjointness_overlap_note: >-
  Data sets may satisfy the hypotheses of more than one descriptor: for example Schwarzschild vacuum
  data also solve the Einstein-massless-scalar-field system with phi = 0 (review HF-04). What is
  exclusive is the class binding of a CLAIM, and a checker must not read this table as data-space
  disjointness. The decisive axes below separate descriptors, not solution sets.
disjointness:
  # Scope note (review HF-04): disjointness is a property of the class DESCRIPTORS, not of the
  # underlying data sets. Data sets may satisfy hypotheses of more than one descriptor
  # (e.g. Schwarzschild vacuum data also solve the scalar system with phi = 0); what is exclusive
  # is the class binding of a CLAIM.
  - pair: ["AF-WCC-VAC-GEN", "AF-SCC-C2-VAC-GEN"]
    decisive_axes: ["family", "regularity_token", "conclusion_type"]
    separation: "WCC asserts visibility/asymptotic predictability with no extension-regularity token; C2-SCC asserts C2-inextendibility. A spacetime may be WCC-consistent while failing C2-SCC (non-generic exact black holes), so the classes are not coextensive."
  - pair: ["AF-WCC-VAC-GEN", "AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN"]
    decisive_axes: ["family", "regularity_token", "conclusion_type"]
    separation: "Same family separation as the C2 pair, with the strictly stronger C0 conclusion."
  - pair: ["AF-WCC-VAC-GEN", "AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH"]
    decisive_axes: ["matter_model", "symmetry"]
    separation: "Vacuum versus massless scalar field, and no symmetry assumption versus spherical symmetry; the data spaces differ, so neither hypotheses nor conclusions transfer."
  - pair: ["AF-SCC-C2-VAC-GEN", "AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN"]
    decisive_axes: ["regularity_token", "conclusion_type"]
    separation: "C0-inextendibility implies C2-inextendibility for identical data and genericity, but not conversely; the conclusions are distinct values and may never be merged into a single regularity token (guards G3)."
  - pair: ["AF-SCC-C2-VAC-GEN", "AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH"]
    decisive_axes: ["family", "matter_model", "symmetry", "conclusion_type"]
    separation: "Conclusion family, matter model and symmetry all differ."
  - pair: ["AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN", "AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH"]
    decisive_axes: ["family", "matter_model", "symmetry", "conclusion_type"]
    separation: "Conclusion family, matter model and symmetry all differ."

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transfer rules. Only one direction is sound; everything else is class leakage
# or conclusion inflation and must be rejected by the downstream linters.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
transfer_rules:
  allowed:
    - id: "T1"
      from: "AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN"
      to: "AF-SCC-C2-VAC-GEN"
      kind: "conclusion_strengthening"
      reason: "If no C0 extension exists, then no C2 extension exists."
      guards:
        - "data_class fields must match exactly (including s, delta once F2 fixes them)"
        - "genericity_kind and genericity_topology must match exactly"
        - "the source claim must carry artifact_refs and a reviewer verdict"
  forbidden:
    - id: "X1"
      pattern: "AF-SCC-C2-VAC-GEN -> AF-SCC-C0-VAC-GEN"
      kind: "conclusion_inflation"
      reason: "A C2-inextendibility result does not imply C0-inextendibility."
    - id: "X2"
      pattern: "AF-WCC-VAC-GEN <-> AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH"
      kind: "matter_leakage"
      reason: "Vacuum and scalar-field data spaces differ; no transfer without a separate bridge lemma artifact."
    - id: "X3"
      pattern: "AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH -> AF-WCC-VAC-GEN (or any class with symmetry: none_assumed)"
      kind: "symmetry_release"
      reason: "Spherical results do not transfer to the unconstrained data space."
    - id: "X4"
      pattern: "any WCC <-> any SCC conclusion"
      kind: "conclusion_family_leakage"
      reason: "Visibility and inextendibility are different conclusions; a bridge lemma must be filed as its own artifact."
    - id: "X5"
      pattern: "any string matching the merged-regularity regex defined in guards G3"
      kind: "class_merge"
      reason: "ASTRA_HANDOFF.md hard decision 1: the classes stay separate."

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-checkable guards for F1/F2/A1 tooling.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
guards:
  - id: "G1"
    rule: "each claim carries exactly one class_id from class_ids"
  - id: "G2"
    rule: "family == SCC implies exactly one regularity_token in {C0, C2}; family == WCC implies regularity_token is absent/null"
  - id: "G3"
    rule: >-
      no merged regularity string matches the normalized pattern. Normalize before matching by removing
      the characters ^ { } _ and whitespace, so that braced/superscript spellings such as C^{{0}} or
      C^{{2}} are caught, not only the plain spelling (review finding 6). The full regex lives in
      artifacts/worker-01/validate_taxonomy.py (MERGED_REGULARITY_RE + normalization) and must be
      copied by downstream linters, not re-derived.
  - id: "G4"
    rule: "no symmetry release: a spherical-symmetry result may not be filed under a none_assumed class"
  - id: "G5"
    rule: "no matter-model swap: vacuum <-> massless_scalar_field without a bridge artifact"
  - id: "G6"
    rule: "no conclusion inflation: C2 result may not be filed as C0; WCC may not be filed as SCC"
  - id: "G7"
    rule: "conclusion_type == theorem requires artifact_refs with sha256 and a reviewer verdict (comms/PROTOCOL.md rule 2)"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Coverage gaps and open questions this file deliberately does not resolve.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage_gaps:
  - id: "CG1"
    text: "AF-WCC-SCALAR-SPH has no schema node (F-node) in research_map.json; F1/F2 cover only the three vacuum classes."
  - id: "CG2"
    text: "No class exists for non-spherical matter models, Lambda != 0, or higher-genus ends; such claims must open a new class rather than be filed here."

open_questions:
  - id: "Q1"
    text: "Which genericity notion (Baire residual, dense open, full measure) and which topology on the weighted Sobolev data space does each WCC/SCC class use? Owned by F1/F2 with L1 input."
  - id: "Q2"
    text: "Exact definition of C0-inextendibility (regularity of metric versus embedding) and its relation to C^{1,1} and H^2_loc formulations. Owned by F2."
  - id: "Q3"
    text: "Does the C0 class's genericity clause exclude exactly the smooth-extension black-hole families, and at which data-space topology does that exclusion hold? Owned by F2/L1."
  - id: "Q4"
    text: "Which literature statements in this file's 'known_obstruction' fields are actually theorems, with primary-source scope quotes and hashes? Owned by L1."

